import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title={"Privacy notice | Change My Name UK"}
  description={"How Change My Name UK uses your information when you use the free checklist, offer to talk to us or apply for the beta."}
  path={"/privacy.html"}
  ogTitle={"Privacy notice"}
>
<main id="main" class="wrap narrow doc">
  <h1>Privacy notice</h1>
  <p>Last updated: 15 November 2026</p>
  <p>This notice explains how we use your information when you use our free checklist, joined our waitlist, offer to talk to us, apply for our beta, or register interest in our deed poll. We'll publish a full privacy notice for customers before the paid service launches.</p>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>Change My Name UK is run by Avi Arnon, a sole trader, of 3 Myddelton Passage, London EC1R 1XW, UK, who is the data controller for your information. We plan to set up a limited company to run the service, and we'll update this notice when we do. ICO registration number: to be added. You can contact us at <a href="mailto:hello@changemynameuk.com">hello@changemynameuk.com</a>.</p>

  <h2>The free checklist</h2>
  <p>The checklist runs in your web browser. Your answers, and the items you tick off, are saved only on your own device (in your browser's local storage) so the list is still there when you come back. They are not sent to us unless you choose to sign in to save them to an account (see "If you create an account" below) or submit one of the forms below. You can clear them at any time by clearing your browser's site data. If you copy a link to your list, the link contains your answers (not your name or email), so only share it with people you're happy to see them.</p>
  <p>If your reason for changing your name is something other than marriage or divorce, we don't ask what it is.</p>

  <h2>What we collect when you send us a form</h2>
  <div class="tbl"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Form</th><th>What we collect</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Waitlist (closed)</td><td>Your email address, and your wedding date if you give it</td><td>To tell you when we launch and send your early-bird offer, timed around your wedding</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Research call sign-up</td><td>Your first name, email address, phone number if you give it, how and when you'd like to talk, which boxes you ticked, and a summary of your checklist answers if you came from the checklist (for example where in the UK you live, how far you've got, and the types of accounts you have, but not account numbers)</td><td>To arrange a research call, prepare for it and send your thank-you voucher. If you ticked the launch box, also to tell you when we launch.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Deed poll interest</td><td>Your first name, email address, where you live, what you're changing, when you need it if you say, and which boxes you ticked</td><td>To email you when you can order a deed poll, and to understand demand. If you ticked the call box, also to arrange a research call.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Old Name Check pilot sign-up</td><td>Your first name, email address, where you are with your divorce, and which boxes you ticked</td><td>To email you when pilot places open, and to arrange a call if you ticked that box. We don't search for anyone until you join the pilot and confirm who you are.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Beta application</td><td>Your first name, email address, reason for the change, where in the UK you live, a date if you give one, how much help you'd want, anything you write in the notes, and your checklist answers if you came from the checklist</td><td>To decide who gets a beta place, contact you about the beta, and understand what people need and would pay. If you ticked the call box, also to arrange a research call.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p>When you submit a form, our hosting provider also records basic technical data, such as the time and your IP address, to block spam. We don't use tracking or advertising cookies on this site.</p>

  <h2 id="accounts">If you create an account</h2>
  <p>You can choose to sign in with your email address so your checklist is saved and you can pick it up on another device. There's no password: we email you a link each time. This is optional and the checklist works without it.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>What we save:</strong> your email address, your checklist answers (for example your reason for changing your name, where in the UK you live, your wedding date if you gave it, and which kinds of accounts you have), and for each organisation or step on your list whether it's still to do, you've asked, it's done or it's confirmed, the date that changed, and how it was confirmed (you ticked it, or a confirmation was found). We also keep a dated history of those changes. If you use the inbox scanner while signed in, we save the same progress details for the organisations in your tracker, your old and new surname if you entered them, and whether each organisation's latest email uses your old or new name. We never save the text of your emails.</li>
    <li><strong>Why:</strong> to keep your progress safe across devices, and so we can see how far you've got and help you with the places that are left, for example when you join our beta. We don't use it for advertising and we never sell it.</li>
    <li><strong>Who can see it:</strong> you, and the founder of Change My Name UK. The database only lets each signed-in person see their own records.</li>
    <li><strong>Where it's stored:</strong> with Supabase, in its London data centre (see "Who we share it with").</li>
    <li><strong>Lawful basis:</strong> your consent, which you give by asking for a sign-in link. You can withdraw it at any time.</li>
    <li><strong>Deleting it:</strong> email <a href="mailto:hello@changemynameuk.com">hello@changemynameuk.com</a> from the address you signed in with and we'll delete your account and everything saved in it within one month. Signing out doesn't delete anything, and the copy in your browser stays until you clear your browser's site data.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Visitor statistics</h2>
  <p>We count visits with Cloudflare Web Analytics so we can see which pages are useful and how people find us. It doesn't use cookies, doesn't store anything on your device and doesn't follow you to other sites. It records things like the page you viewed, the site that sent you, and your browser and country. We only see totals, not individual visitors. Our lawful basis is our legitimate interest in understanding how the site is used.</p>
  <p>Please don't include health information or other sensitive details in the notes box. We don't need them.</p>

  <h2>Our lawful basis</h2>
  <p>We rely on your <strong>consent</strong>, which you give by submitting a form and ticking the boxes that apply. Each tick box is separate and none is ticked for you. You can withdraw your consent at any time by replying "unsubscribe" to any email or emailing us, and we'll stop contacting you.</p>

  <h2>Research calls</h2>
  <p>If you agree to a call, it will be with the founder by phone or video and will take about 15 minutes. If you book through our booking page, the booking provider will also receive your name, email and chosen time. We may take notes. We'll only record a call if you agree at the start. We use what we learn to design the service, and if we ever quote you, we won't name you. We send your thank-you voucher to the email address you gave us.</p>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>We don't sell your details or share them for anyone else's marketing. We use these service providers:</p>
  <div class="tbl"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Provider</th><th>What they do</th><th>Where</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Netlify, Inc.</td><td>Hosts this website and stores form submissions</td><td>United States</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Cloudflare, Inc.</td><td>Counts visits to the website (no cookies)</td><td>United States</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Supabase, Inc.</td><td>Stores customer accounts and saved progress, and sends sign-in emails</td><td>United Kingdom (London data centre); Supabase is a US company</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p>Where your data is processed outside the UK, it's protected by the UK Extension to the EU-US Data Privacy Framework or by the UK International Data Transfer Addendum to standard contractual clauses.</p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Waitlist and launch updates: until you unsubscribe, or for up to 12 months after the service launches if you haven't become a customer, whichever is sooner.</li>
    <li>Accounts and saved progress: until you ask us to delete them, or 12 months after you last signed in, whichever is sooner.</li>
    <li>Research call contacts, call notes, beta applications and deed poll interest: up to 12 months after we collect them, unless you become a customer, when our customer privacy notice will apply. Anonymised notes may be kept longer.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under UK data protection law you can ask to see the data we hold about you, correct it, delete it, restrict or object to how we use it, or receive a copy to move elsewhere. Email us and we'll reply within one month.</p>
  <p>If you're unhappy with how we've handled your data, please tell us first. You can also complain to the Information Commissioner's Office at <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint</a> or on 0303 123 1113.</p>

  <p><a href="/">Back to the home page</a></p>
</main>
</Base>
